The claim 'Something began affecting major airlines on a specific Friday.' is supported by the citation.
<accept> The article explicitly states in the headline and several times within the body that a "global tech outage" or "technology meltdown" "hit Friday" and that the "outage began Friday," affecting airlines worldwide. </accept>

**********Source Check**********

The claim 'Someone stated that a recent weekend was the busiest travel weekend of the summer.' is supported by the citation.
<accept> The article states that "Delta CEO Ed Bastian" said, "The technology issue occurred on the busiest travel weekend of the summer, with our booked loads exceeding 90%, limiting our reaccommodation capabilities." This directly matches the information provided. </accept>

**********Exact Claim Check**********

The claim 'Southwest experienced a major operational disruption in December 2022.' is supported by the original webpage.
<accept> The content explicitly states that "It happened to Southwest during peak holiday travel time in December 2022 when severe winter storms forced airlines to cancel droves of flights. But, as the weather improved, thousands of Southwest planes remained grounded for an infamous 10 days even as just about every other airline was operating without major disruptions." This clearly describes a major operational disruption for Southwest in December 2022. </accept>

**********Exact Claim Check**********

The claim 'A CrowdStrike outage began affecting major airlines on a specific Friday.' is supported by the original webpage.
<accept> The content explicitly states: "Now, in the wake of the CrowdStrike outage that began affecting major airlines on Friday, many across the globe that were initially prevented from flying had recovered and resumed normal operations by the end of the weekend." This confirms that a CrowdStrike outage began affecting major airlines on a specific Friday. </accept>

**********Exact Claim Check**********

The claim 'Delta CEO Ed Bastian stated that a recent weekend was the busiest travel weekend of the summer.' is supported by the original webpage.
<accept> The text states, "And it just so happened to be that the past weekend was the busiest travel weekend of the summer, Delta CEO Ed Bastian said in a recent note." This directly supports the claim. </accept>

